==English==
{{was wotd|2018|December|24}}

===Etymology===
{{multiple images
|direction = vertical
|image1 = Le bacche del vischio.jpg
|caption1 = A [[European mistletoe]] (''[[Viscum album]]''; ''sense 1'') plant
|image2 = Woolson Spice Co. (3092983603).jpg
|caption2 = A [[Victorian]] [[trade card]] depicting mistletoe hung up as a [[Christmas]] [[decoration]] ''(sense 2)'', with two people [[kiss#Verb|kissing]] beneath it
}}

From {{inh|en|enm|mistelto}}, {{m|enm|mistilto|t=European mistletoe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|misteltān}}, {{m|ang|mistiltān|t=mistletoe}}, from {{m|ang|mistel|t=mistletoe; basil; birdlime}} + {{m|ang|tān|t=sprig, shoot, twig}} (which was mistaken for the plural of {{m|ang|tā|t=toe}}),<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=mistel-tō|part of speech=n|id=MED28273|accessdate=19 July 2018}}</ref> equivalent to {{com|en|mistle|tan|t2=twig|nocat=1}}, possibly as a {{calque|ang|non|mistilteinn|nocat=1|nocap=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|da|mistelten|t=mistletoe}}, {{cog|no|misteltein|t=mistletoe}}, {{cog|is|mistilteinn|t=mistletoe}}. Compare also the simplex form {{cog|fy|mistel|t=mistletoe}}, {{cog|nl|mistel|t=mistletoe}}, {{cog|de|Mistel|t=mistletoe}}, {{cog|sv|mistel|t=mistletoe}}.

